# Gitignored files copied into worktrees managed by Claude Code and the local
# Codex desktop app. Claude Code uses this for `--worktree`, `EnterWorktree`, and
# isolated subagents; Codex uses it for chats started in Worktree mode. Both copy
# a path only when it is listed here AND gitignored, so tracked files cannot be
# pulled in by accident. Syntax is .gitignore's.
#
# Keep this to per-checkout *configuration*. Each isolated Claude subagent or
# Codex worktree chat can get a separate checkout, so every entry may be fanned
# out across dozens of directories: a credential must never be listed, and
# neither must a file that points at one.

# The code-review plugin's local overrides. A worktree without them falls back to
# the committed .reviewer/settings.json, whose verify_conversation source list is
# far wider than one session's transcripts.
.reviewer/settings.local.json

# Claude permissions and env already granted for this checkout, so an isolated
# Claude agent does not re-prompt for each one.
.claude/settings.local.json

# Deliberately NOT listed: .mngr/settings.local.toml. Its `env_file` is a
# repo-relative .env holding a GitHub token -- copying the pointer alone leaves a
# create-template that fails on use, and copying both would spread the token into
# every agent worktree.
